ColorSchemes.NoteTitle = How this page writes
ColorSchemes.NoteIntro = Two files are involved, and they are not the same kind of thing:
ColorSchemes.NoteInject = Scheme definitions are injected as patch/preset_color_schemes/<id>. This page only ever touches ids it created itself — schemes you wrote by hand are left untouched.
ColorSchemes.NoteSwitch = style/color_scheme decides which scheme is in use. That key belongs to the Appearance page; this page only reads it to show the “in use” badge. Two pages must never fight over the same key.
ColorSchemes.NoteFormat = Byte order is stored per scheme. Switching it rewrites every literal, so the colours stay the same — 0x112233 in abgr becomes 0x332211 in argb, not a different colour.
ColorSchemes.NoteDeploy = Saving only writes the files. Press Deploy (or redeploy from Weasel's menu) to make the new scheme take effect.

