# ── Behavior page ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Behavior.Switch.Title = Chinese / English switch
Behavior.Switch.Intro = What each of these five keys does when pressed. Written to the ascii_composer section of default.custom.yaml.
Behavior.GoodOldCapsLock = Caps Lock commits ASCII directly (good_old_caps_lock)
Behavior.GoodOldCapsLock.Note = When on, letters typed while Caps Lock is lit go straight to the screen without passing through the candidate window. When off, each key follows the action picked below. This is Rime's factory default.
Behavior.SwitchKey.CapsLock = Caps Lock
Behavior.SwitchKey.ShiftL = Left Shift
Behavior.SwitchKey.ShiftR = Right Shift
Behavior.SwitchKey.ControlL = Left Control
Behavior.SwitchKey.ControlR = Right Control
Behavior.Switch.Note = "Not set" leaves that key out of the config, so the scheme's own default still applies. If every key is "Not set" the panel deletes the switch_key entry entirely rather than writing an empty map — an empty map tells Rime "the user explicitly declared there are no switch keys", which also disables the ones the scheme ships with.
Behavior.SwitchAction.Unset = Not set (keep scheme default)
Behavior.SwitchAction.inline_ascii = Type ASCII inline — letters show as you type and commit without the candidate window
Behavior.SwitchAction.commit_code = Commit the raw code (the letters you typed)
Behavior.SwitchAction.commit_text = Commit the raw candidate text (the pinyin string)
Behavior.SwitchAction.clear = Clear the input buffer (throw away what you typed)
Behavior.SwitchAction.noop = Do nothing (swallow the key)
Behavior.Candidate.Title = Candidate window behavior
Behavior.Candidate.Intro = Weasel-specific settings. Written to weasel.custom.yaml.
Behavior.PagingOnScroll = Page with the mouse wheel
Behavior.PagingOnScroll.Note = While candidates are on screen, the wheel pages through them instead of scrolling the page underneath.
Behavior.ClickToCapture = Capture the mouse when clicking the candidate window
Behavior.ClickToCapture.Note = Stops a click on a candidate from also reaching the window behind it.
Behavior.VerticalAutoReverse = Auto-flip when vertical
Behavior.VerticalAutoReverse.Note = In vertical layout, the window flips to the other side of the caret when it gets close to the screen edge.
Behavior.Status.Title = Status & tips
Behavior.GlobalAscii = Global ASCII mode (global_ascii)
Behavior.GlobalAscii.Note = One shared Chinese/English state across all programs. Uncheck it and every window remembers its own state.
Behavior.AsciiTipFollowCursor = ASCII tip follows the caret
Behavior.AsciiTipFollowCursor.Note = Show a small hint next to the caret when you switch. Uncheck it to show the hint at a fixed spot on screen.
Behavior.DisplayTrayIcon = Show the tray icon
Behavior.DisplayTrayIcon.Note = Show the Weasel icon in the notification area. Requires a redeploy after changing.
Behavior.Notify.Title = Notifications
Behavior.ShowNotifications = Show notifications
Behavior.NotifyTime = Duration
Behavior.NotifyTime.Unit = ms
Behavior.Notify.Note = The toast shown when switching schemes, finishing a deploy, and so on. 0 means use the system default.
Behavior.Apply.Title = Apply
Behavior.Apply.Note = Writes weasel.custom.yaml and default.custom.yaml. default.custom.yaml is edited line by line, so anything else you hand-wrote in that file — including comments — is preserved. Press "Deploy" on the Appearance page afterwards.
